    "description": "On site descriptive sign (translation from Japanese) \nRemains of the garden of rest for wild eagles.\nA place of rest for young pilots who had completed flight training during the war. It was a place where kamikaze pilots could rest before heading to their bases near the end of the war. Previously, a wooden sign reading \"The Pond Where Eagles Rest\" had been erected. There are traces of a pond that has been hardened by cleats.\nAccording to one theory, the money was donated by young kamikaze pilots.\nMarch 2022\nTokorozawa City\n\nTokorozawa Aviation Materials Research and Collection Association",
